# Populum Modding

This workspace is the live Populum mod for Conquest of Elysium 5.

## Mod structure

- **Steam publish folder:** `populum/` (only this folder is uploaded to Workshop)
- Primary mod file: `populum/populum.c5m` (~90k lines)
- Assets: `populum/pop/` (sprites, banners, map tiles)
- Custom map: `populum/GOTcoe5.coem`
- Steam Workshop: `populum/coe5ws.txt`, `populum/steam_descr.txt`, `populum/banner.png`
- Dev tooling (repo root, not published): `py_tools/`, `art_tools/`, `tools/`, `.vscode/`, `.cursor/`
- Sprite batch pipeline: `art_tools/` (ComfyUI scan/generate; outputs land in `populum/pop/`)
- Helper scripts: `py_tools/pop_hp.py`, `py_tools/gainrit_describer.py`, `py_tools/gainrit_distance.py`, `py_tools/gainrit_validator.py`, `py_tools/validate_populum.py`, `py_tools/extract_modding_manual.py`
- Extracted manual rules: `py_tools/references/coe5_modding_rules.json`, `py_tools/references/coe5_command_index.json`

Modding reference: https://illwinter.com/coe5/coe5modding.html (use `extract_modding_manual.py lookup --command-index` before editing commands)

## Command execution order

Commands in `.c5m` files run top-to-bottom. Prerequisites must appear before dependents (e.g. define weapons before assigning them to monsters).

## Save compatibility (critical)

When updating existing content, **append only** new units, classes, rituals, weapons, and terrain at the **end** of their respective sections. Inserting new definitions in the middle shuffles IDs and breaks saved games.

**Appending `newritual` at the end is safe for save games but still shifts the global ritual index** used by `gainrit` offsets on every line that points forward to a mod ritual. Always run gainrit validation after any `newritual` add, remove, or reorder (see below).

## Ritual power placement (ritpow vs newritpow)

- **`newritpow`** — creates a mod-original ritual school. All rituals belonging to that school go immediately after its `newritpow` line (until the next `newritpow`). Do **not** use explicit `ritpow <n>` for mod-created schools.
- **`ritpow <n>`** — only when adding rituals to an **existing vanilla** school. Verify the number in `py_tools/references/Ritual Data v5.33.c5m` or the modding manual ritual-school table (e.g. `ritpow 48 # Scourge Lord`).
- **Never** append mod-school rituals at the file end with `ritpow <mod_index>` as a shortcut — insert them in the correct `newritpow` block instead.
- After any ritual add/move/remove, run `validate_populum.py --fix --describe`.

## Gainrit validation (required after ritual changes)

CoE5 resolves `gainrit <offset>` against the **global ritual list**: vanilla `newritual` entries first, then every Populum `newritual` in file order. Adding or removing a mod ritual changes all later indices; stale offsets grant the wrong ritual with no in-game error.

After **any** edit that adds, removes, or moves a `newritual` block in `populum/populum.c5m`:

```bash
python py_tools/validate_populum.py --fix --describe
```

- **`--fix`** — rewrite offsets to match trailing `# "Target Ritual"` comments (keep those comments accurate when editing)
- **`--describe`** — refresh describer comments after offset fixes or new `gainrit` lines
- Must exit **0** before considering the mod change complete

Validate only (no file writes):

```bash
python py_tools/validate_populum.py
```

VS Code/Cursor: **Tasks → Run Test Task → Validate Populum (gainrit)** or **Validate Populum (fix + describe)**.

Offset lookup between two rituals: `python py_tools/gainrit_distance.py "Source Ritual" "Target Ritual"` (add `--gui` for the interactive window).

## Vanilla reference data (read-only)

Look up names and stats in `py_tools/references/` before inventing duplicates:

- `Monster Data v5.33.c5m`
- `Class Data v5.33.c5m`
- `Ritual Data v5.33.c5m`
- `Weapon Data v5.33.c5m`
- `Terrain Data v5.33.c5m`
- `Magic Item Data v5.33.c5m`
- `Recruitment Data v5.33.c5m`

Never edit reference files as part of Populum changes.

## Editing discipline

- Minimize diffs in the monolithic `populum/populum.c5m`; avoid unrelated reformatting
- Preserve filename case for TGA/PNG assets (Linux and Steam Workshop are case-sensitive)
- Graphics: 24- or 32-bit TGA or PNG in `populum/pop/`

## Monster weapon commands (damage bonus required)

CoE5 weapon lines always lead with a **damage bonus**, then the weapon (name or numeric id). Omitting the bonus defaults to **-1 damage**.

```text
rangedweapon 0 "Crossbow"      # +0 bonus (standard crossbow damage)
rangedweapon 0   9             # +0 bonus, weapon id 9 (Crossbow)
meleeweapon  2   3             # +2 bonus, weapon id 3 (Axe)
meleeweaponbonus 2 "Grapple"   # +2 bonus named weapon
rangedweapon50 0 "Throwing Dagger"
```

**Wrong:** `rangedweapon "Crossbow"` — applies -1 damage penalty.

When editing or adding weapons, check vanilla stats in `py_tools/references/Monster Data v5.33.c5m` for the intended bonus, or use `0` for standard weapon damage. Lookup: `python py_tools/extract_modding_manual.py lookup --command-index rangedweapon`.

## Sprite references and batch generation

When adding **new original** mod content that needs graphics, **include the sprite path in `.c5m` even if the image file does not exist yet**. Missing files are expected during authoring; they are filled in later by the `art_tools/` batch pipeline.

- **`newmonster`:** set `spr1` (and `spr2` after `spr1` when attack art differs). Use paths under `pop/` (e.g. `spr1 "pop/monster/myunit01.tga"`, `spr2 "pop/monster/myunit02.tga"`).
- **`newitem`:** set `spr "pop/item/myitem.tga"`.
- **`selectterr` / `newterr`:** set `spr "pop/map/mytile.tga"`.
- Do **not** omit sprite lines or defer them because the TGA/PNG is missing.
- Do **not** block `.c5m` edits waiting for art; pick stable final filenames up front (case-sensitive for Workshop/Linux).

After sprite paths exist in the mod file, generate missing assets with:

```bash
python art_tools/comfyui_run_sprites.py --scan populum/populum.c5m
python art_tools/comfyui_run_sprites.py --jobs art_tools/generated/missing_sprites_jobs.json --resume
```

Style tuning (once): `python art_tools/comfyui_probe_sprite_styles.py --resume`, then set `art_tools/coe5_probe_winners.json`.

## Testing

Edits in this folder are picked up by CoE5 immediately after save. Enable the Populum mod in-game and restart if the mod list was open during editing.
